# `build:single` inlines index.html verbatim into hitstop.html, so the two
# must agree on line endings or every rebuild rewrites the wrapper — and
# rule 5 says rebuild the committed bundle on every game change, which
# turns that into constant noise.
#
# The pairing is deliberate, and not symmetric:
#
#   index.html   LF   — the build's INPUT. vite-plugin-singlefile removes
#                       the <script> line and does not take the newline
#                       before it with it, so a CRLF source leaves a stray
#                       CR: `</div>\r` + CRLF. Git's clean filter then
#                       stores that first CR as CONTENT, and no checkout
#                       can round-trip it — a fresh clone is dirty the
#                       moment anything re-stats the file. Feed the build
#                       LF and the artifact never appears.
#   hitstop.html CRLF — the build's OUTPUT, and what the committed bundle
#                       has always carried. Stored LF, checked out CRLF on
#                       every platform.
index.html   text eol=lf
hitstop.html text eol=crlf
